<title>TURKEY: Southbound traffic resumes on Bosphorus strait.</title>
<headline>Southbound traffic resumes on Bosphorus strait.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bosphorus strait was reopened to southbound traffic at midday on Friday local time as fog lifted, maritime officials said.</p>
<p>The narrow waterway has been closed to two-way traffic due to dense fog since early hours on Thursday, causing more than 100 vessels to accumulate at each end of the strait.</p>
<p>Officials said northbound crossing would resume after most southbound vessels pass.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
